# The distributions this project publishes a preset for.
#
# One line per preset, in the same field order and with the same separator the
# upstream's own index uses, because every line here is looked up in that index:
#
#   preset;distro;release;variant
#
# The preset name is what a user writes in values.yaml, and the three fields
# after it are what identify the build on images.linuxcontainers.org. The name is
# not derived from them - `voidlinux;current` reads as `void-current` to a person
# and nothing should have to know that rule twice.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for what exists. The build matrix, the
# daily bump, the retention job and `hack/check-presets.sh` all read it, so a
# preset added here and nowhere else is built, published, kept up to date and
# checked against the shipped catalog without any of them being edited.
#
# The variant is `default` for every preset and is written out anyway. The
# upstream also publishes `cloud` and `tinycloud` variants, which carry cloud-init
# that this chart does not drive, and Void publishes a `musl` variant. Leaving the
# field implicit would make adding one of those look like a smaller decision than
# it is.
#
# Adding a release is a line. Removing one is a line and a catalog entry, and
# stops the daily bump proposing it - it does not withdraw what is already
# published, because a machine's source has to stay resolvable.
debian-trixie;debian;trixie;default
ubuntu-noble;ubuntu;noble;default
alpine-3.24;alpine;3.24;default
void-current;voidlinux;current;default
